Package: shinyEncrypt
Title: Multi-Step File Conversion and Cryptographic Protection (Shiny)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("YH", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "lauyeehow1986@gmail.com")
Description: A Shiny application and cryptographic engine that converts CSV/XLSX
    (or existing RDS/binary) data into a serialized, Base64-encoded payload and
    protects it with standard and state-of-the-art cryptography. Users adjust
    parameters live, export a reproducible R script and/or a ciphertext text
    envelope, download the relevant key material, and decrypt artifacts back to
    the original binary. A companion native package binds Rust/C/C++ crates for
    post-quantum, homomorphic and advanced primitives (optional).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    shiny,
    bslib,
    sodium,
    openssl,
    digest,
    jsonlite,
    readr,
    readxl,
    zip,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    shinyEncryptPRE
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
